{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CONFIRMING EVIDENCE from Gerrit change 1577 (bug 85fa) — this is exactly the case in the title.\n\nLLM-Review voted -1 with the bugfix-size-attestation finding: 321 non-test lines, over the\n150-line bugfix floor, and bug 85fa had no plan-review attestation. I then EARNED the\nattestation (rebar review-plan 85fa -> PASS, after correcting the ticket description). The\nblocking condition was gone — but the vote could not be recomputed.\n\nFour re-trigger paths, all swallowed by the copy condition\n  ('changekind:NO_CODE_CHANGE OR changekind:MERGE_FIRST_PARENT_UPDATE OR TRIVIAL_REBASE'):\n  1. git commit --amend --no-edit + push   -> same tree AND message -> NO_CODE_CHANGE -> copied\n  2. commit-MESSAGE-only amend + push      -> tree unchanged        -> NO_CODE_CHANGE -> copied\n  3. recheck-review comment                -> no reviewer response (see bug b0f5: fire-and-\n                                              forget into a volatile queue) AND it cancelled\n                                              the in-flight CI run (see bug 0d78)\n  4. rebase onto current main + push       -> TRIVIAL_REBASE -> copied\n\nCI behaves correctly by contrast — Verified re-ran on patch sets 3 and 4. Only the LLM review\nis stuck, which makes the asymmetry easy to misread as 'the review just has not run yet'.\n\nWHY THE COPY CONDITION IS WRONG FOR THIS FINDING SPECIFICALLY: bugfix-size-attestation's\nevidence lives OUTSIDE the diff — it is attestation state on the TICKET. NO_CODE_CHANGE is a\nsound reason to copy a finding about the CODE; it is unsound for a finding about the world\naround the code, which can change without the tree changing. That distinction may be a\ncleaner fix than making recheck-review special-case this one finding.\n\nCost observed: the change was unlandable on its own merits until a maintainer intervened, and\nthe detour also produced a spurious Verified -1 from the cancelled CI run.\n\n(I filed 9b70 before finding this ticket — closing that as a duplicate of this one.)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786377092683755001,"uuid":"d8c91a6d-cb5d-4354-a82d-36233d54d404"}